  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Line-transect Survey of Marine Mammals of the SE Bering Sea",
  "description": "During June 1999, we will conduct a line transect survey of marine mammals in conjunction with NOAA/AFSC/MACE cruise dedicated to hydroacoustic assessments of pollock in the Bering Sea. A mesoscale synoptic and will cross the shelf from outer Bristol Bay to west of the Pribilof Islands, extending as far as the Inner Front (50 misobath) on the shelf. A single towed hydrophone (200 Hz to 22khz and 30 kHz to 150 kHz) with collect acoustic data. Air and information (ocean temperature, salinity, chlorophyll content) [ An NPMR project ] [ Reference: Tynan, C.T. 2004. Cetacean populations on the southeastern Bering Sea shelf during the late 1990s: Implications for decadal changes in ecosystem structure and carbon flow. Marine Ecology Progress Series (in press) ]\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Data supporting NPMR project \"Oceanographic and ecological factors influencing the occurrence patterns of whales in the Southeast Bering Sea\"",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23506961",
